I've tried to use the graphics and standout options with Nethack 3.0g
Patchlevel 5 with no success.  I didn't muck with any of the termcap
or terminfo definitions in config.h when I installed it on a NeXT
running its (supposedly) BSD4.3 Unix Mach 1.0.  Everything seems
to work as far as cursor positioning goes, but the AS and AE, and	
SO and SE (I assume for standout) codes get ignored.  The only way
I can get the meta characters to show up is to do an stty raw before
executing nethack, and then I get the IBM PC graphic characters
rather than the vt102 line drawing characters.  I've double checked
my vt102 emulation in MS-Kermit 2.32/A and it works fine if I send
it the control codes with echo, and in debug mode I can see that
everything is generated except the four codes I mentioned above.

Has anyone had any luck with this?  It would also be nice to allow
the color codes in the Unix version that Kermit supports as an
extension to the vt102 code set (ANSI SGR).  It would really be
nice if I could tell which monster was my tame little dog, and which
of the other three d's were those nasty jackals!
(option  color:33:31:32   tame monster: artifacts: other monsters)

So far, I've not gotten past level nine, but I don't think it is the
fault of the new game, I just assume I'm back to the botton of the
learning curve again.  It took me a year of playing the original
Kneller port of hack for the IBM PC before I could escape the dungeon
with the amulet, so I figure a few weeks of acting like a neophyte
again isn't so bad.

Strength seems to be much more of a problem than it used to be for
my favorite character the archeologist.  With out potions of gain
strength, and running into killer bees on level three long before
I can get near some royal jelly, I find I've lost all my strength
pretty quick in a lot of games.

I know about gain ability, but the odds of getting strength from
one are pretty low.  This is a crisis I don't know how to avoid.
Even if one tries to avoid hand to hand combat with killer bees,
there are usually too many around to even make it off the level once
they are encountered.

